# {{.App}}

A SvelteKit application served by Go. VitePlus and `sv` created the frontend;
skgo added the Go server and bindings. Production needs no Node at request time; development uses Vite/Kit.

## Prerequisites

- Go {{.GoVersion}} or newer for production builds; exactly Go 1.27.2 for `skgo dev`
- Node 22.17 or newer
- VitePlus 1.0.0 (`vp`) and `just`

The generator installed frontend dependencies and made an initial frontend
build{{if .ComponentTests}}, and installed Chromium for Vitest component tests{{end}}.
These outputs are not committed. In a fresh clone, run:

```sh
just install
just serve
```

Open {{.Origin}}. `just serve` generates bindings, builds the frontend and
runs the standalone Go binary. Rebuild after edits with `just build`.
Run `go tool skgo dev` from the application root for native Kit development
rendering, frontend HMR and native Go updates. Development currently accepts only
macOS ARM64 and Linux AMD64, builds the Go host without cgo, and requires Node
while running. Other platforms and Go versions are rejected at startup.
Compatible Go edits update the running host; changes classified as requiring a
full rebuild replace it and may reset in-memory Go state. Native-loader errors
can instead report a diagnostic and keep serving old code without an automatic
rebuild. Recovery from an observed `R_ADDROFF` relocation failure has not been
verified. Browser draft preservation and full browser-suite coverage
of this development topology are not established. Direct SSR subfetch response
cookies over the private Go socket are not automatically relayed to the page
response. Check authentication in both development and production; see
[skgo's development limitations](https://github.com/tylergannon/skgo#development).

`NewDevelopmentHandler` and
`NewHandler` share the application's setup in `server.go`; the explicit
`*skgo.NativeDevelopment` selects rendering through `development.NewSSR` and
`development.NewStaticHandler`. A nil value selects production Go/goja rendering.
Keep those entry points together when changing the application stack.
{{if .ComponentTests}}
Component tests additionally need `vp exec playwright install chromium` from `web/`.
{{end}}
The project includes skgo's Kit 3.0.0 prerender queue correction in its package
configuration. VitePlus applies it during installation. For an existing app,
run `go tool skgo kit-patch --web web --apply` from the Go app root, then
`vp install --no-frozen-lockfile` from `web/`, followed by
`go tool skgo kit-patch --web web --check` from the app root.

Storybook and Vitest are ready to run:

```sh
just storybook
just test
```

## Production

```sh
just build
./bin/{{.App}}
```

The resulting binary embeds the frontend build and serves it without Node.
From `web/`, `vp run preview` runs `just serve` and previews that same Go binary.
{{if .Examples}}
## Go examples

The home page calls the query and command in
`web/src/routes/example.remote.go`. `skgo generate` creates the matching
TypeScript module with throwing server stubs, so the displayed status and the
write interaction can only be answered by Go.
{{end}}
